      {
        "id": 23891,
        "name": "The Conscience",
        "username": "The_Conscience",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/t/58956e/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2011-11-03T12:11:13.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"&quot;&quot;xBlackWolfx&quot;&quot;\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n \"\"xBlackWolfx\"\":</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I see alot of villain cards have this, ‘draw cards until you find an X card’. but it makes no mention of what to do with all the cards you drew that wasnt what you were looking for. are they discarded, played, or simply shuffled back into the deck?</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>I would say that they would be shuffled back into the deck or discard pile that the villain drew from. It should say on the card itself but if it soes not that would be how I would handle it…In most cases the Villain will shuffle the discard and draw from that until a certain card is found then all the cards are placed in the discard pile face-up next to the draw deck once more.</p>\n<p>Which card are you referring to specifically so we can help you better?</p>",
